@title Trick Star (Europe) (En,Fr,De,Es,It)
@file Trickstar (E) (M5).gba
@game B9SP
@chip EEPROM 4Kbit
@frozen dingbat-bios,mgba,nba
# Language select: English (the default, A; the choice is written to the
# EEPROM at once, 87 bytes), title, new game, slot 1, main menu, League Mode,
# Sam Kisake, the ibex fk 10 bike: reaching the Ibex League screen writes the
# slot (byte 7 and the checksum at 117 change). Egyptron, Now up..., the
# grid; A is held only from 300 frames after the start (a held A through the
# countdown gives mgba a boost start alone) and the race is left 300 frames
# later. [load]: language, title, game select with load game lit, A, the
# slot list (1: Ibex League - Egyptron, Sam with the red bike), A, main menu.
# [load] was resolved on dingbat-bios and mgba only: nba does not recognise
# the save it wrote itself. It writes the 4 Kbit EEPROM's data into an
# 8192-byte file (the first 512 bytes equal the other two's 512-byte files),
# and booted with that file it shows load game greyed out and the slot list
# as New game / slot is empty (f1662, f1848), so its own-save [load] cell
# follows a new game, and booting changes its file (load nba-in-nba
# unchanged=False). dingbat and mgba read nba's 8192-byte file as the save
# (their nba-save cells match their own-save runs).
# Seen while authoring:
# - Language select (f900 on, static): the unselected names are OBJ-mode-1
#   letters (palette 14, colour 0x0017) over BG3's box (palette 44, 0x62F2),
#   BLDCNT 0x1840, BLDALPHA 0x0808. dingbat draws (23,0,0)+(18,23,24) as
#   (20,11,12) and the white 0x7FFF letters as (24,27,27), the 5-bit
#   min(31,(a*8+b*8)>>4); both references draw (21,11,12) and (25,27,28),
#   which is that sum taken on 8-bit expanded channels (x<<3|x>>2). 1700
#   pixels; dingbat's rounding is the one docs/hwprobe-questions.md has from
#   the SP photographs (colour special effects rounding).
# - The race clock starts at a different frame on each emulator: at f3654
#   dingbat-bios reads 0:04:68, mgba 0:04:80, nba 0:04:64, so the countdown
#   ends about 7 frames earlier on mgba and 2 later on nba than on dingbat;
#   with A held through the countdown only mgba gets the boost start (167
#   kph against 80 and 78). With A held from f3654 the bike's speed and line
#   agree on dingbat-bios and mgba; nba's speed reads 2-3 kph apart (f3804
#   146 against 149) and the three drift apart once the bike touches a wall.

[new]
wait 300
wait 300
wait 300
wait 300
checkpoint language window=30
press A
wait 120
wait 120
checkpoint title window=30
press START
wait 90
wait 60
press A
wait 120
checkpoint slot_select window=30
press A
wait 120
checkpoint main_menu window=30
press A
wait 120
checkpoint character_select window=30
press A
wait 120
press A
wait 150
checkpoint league window=30
press A
wait 200
wait 200
wait 60
press A
wait 200
checkpoint race_start window=30
wait 300
hold A
wait 300
checkpoint racing window=30
release

[load]
wait 300
wait 300
wait 300
wait 300
wait 60
press A
wait 120
wait 120
wait 60
press START
wait 90
checkpoint game_select window=30
press A
wait 120
checkpoint load_slots window=30
press A
wait 120
checkpoint main_menu window=30
